Atypical visual novel with effective soundtrack and a good taste in narration. Poor player freedom, but a recommended for the lovers of the genre. Low ecchi content.
Pros:
+ the narrator (the writers, in fact) analyse and express human thoughts and emotions in such a realistic way that the suspension of disbelief is often complete;
+ a lot of different endings;
+ the facial expressions of the NPCs are so weird they always manage to make you smile;
+ somewhat well-rounded characters;
+ erotic content is limited and blended in a mostly sensible way with the plot.
+ interesting references to URSS and Russian culture (at least for an "outlander").
Cons:
- the graphic style and the plot are URSS-inspired: if you are sensitive in this topic avoid the game;
- player has often little choice and sometimes the hints are misleading;
- "punitive": miss a right choice and your struggle for a good end will be in vain (and you won't know it until the end).
[Edit]
- the CGs (gallery) often display different art styles even for the same heroine or scene: while this can make sense in some cases, here it seems that different hands have painted the CGs, which results in an unpleasant feeling of "broken puzzle". That's a shame.

